From fd183402a70cb33b2d5e321e5594cac6e04c7351 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:37:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Essay gate: validate-essays.mjs, and the em-dash and voice
 ratchets cover client/public/essays (U03)

A rewrite turns a pending shelf essay public the moment its file lands, so
every file in client/public/essays now passes a gate before readers see it.

scripts/validate-essays.mjs checks the override shape (the same rule
build-essays-index reads) and no unknown field, second H1, or opening that
repeats the excerpt; Forbidden Language and the essay brief's rulebook
leakage in our own prose; no em-dash in our prose, nor "---", "--", or a
spaced en-dash in its place, and none at all in title or excerpt; an
exclamation point only inside quoted Scripture with its reference beside it;
internal links only to public pages, never through a redirect; at least one
Scripture reference; and Closing Texts as *"Quote."* (Reference) on one line.

A quotation keeps its own words and punctuation (ESV Philemon 16 and the
Whitehead and Perry definition in the pilots carry em-dashes), so the checks
read the prose around quotations (scripts/lib/essay-text.mjs). References
are recognized by shape, not parsed; U09 and U27 tighten that later.

validate-no-emdash.mjs and validate-grow-voice.mjs now include the essays
folder with the same quotation rule. Grow voice's Forbidden Language list
moved unchanged to scripts/lib/forbidden-language.mjs so both gates read one
list, and it loads the Bible only when a BSB-checked file needs it. Both take
--essays <dir> for the seeded-file test. The gate joins the CI content-gates
step; CLAUDE.md's validator list says 23.

server/essay-gate.test.ts: the three gates pass on the committed folder and
on a seeded clean essay, and fail a seeded bad one naming each fault.

